<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <ScenTitle>Wolf Pack</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Date/Time:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;8th May,&amp;nbsp;1982 / 05:00:00 Zulu&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Location:&lt;/STRONG&gt; Falklands - South Atlantic&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Duration:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;12 Hours&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/STRONG&gt; United Kingdom&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;[Hypothetical]&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;What if the remaining Argentine submarines were fully operational at the start of the Falklands War?&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;ARA San Luis, Salta and the recently re-activated ARA Santiago del Estero (sister to the scuttled Santa Fe) have re-deployed to the East of the Falklands to try and engage and sink the British aircraft carriers.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The UK Task Group has retired to the East of the Falklands for refueling and maintenace during the night, before conducting further operations.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Scenario Author: The Stig&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Historical Outcome (SPOILER)&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;EM&gt;ARA San Luis was the target of a number of aggressive ASW attacks on May 1st and again on 10th. The frigates Brilliant and Yarmouth, along with three Sea Kings , conducted a day-long effort. A suspected oil slick was detected, and the British claimed to have damaged or sunk he. Actually she survived the war and afterwards a malfunction on her torpedo maintenance during the war was discovered.&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;EM&gt;ARA San Salta was alongside throughout the War due to engineering defects.&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;EM&gt;ARA Santiago del Estero was alongside due to defects and unable to dive.&lt;/EM&gt;</ScenDescription>
